The King is a 2019 epic historical drama film directed by David Michôd,
based on several plays from William Shakespeare's Henriad.

12
01:28:25,263 --> 01:28:31,263
The screenplay was written by Michôd and Joel Edgerton, who both produced the
film with Brad Pitt, Dede Gardner, Jeremy Kleiner, and Liz Watts.

13
01:35:47,368 --> 01:35:53,368
The King includes an ensemble cast led by Timothée Chalamet as the Prince of Wales and later King Henry V of
England, alongside Edgerton, Sean Harris, Lily-Rose Depp, Robert Pattinson, and Ben Mendelsohn.

14
01:43:09,473 --> 01:43:15,473
The film focuses on the rise of Henry V as king after his father dies as he also must navigate palace
politics, the war his father left behind, and the emotional strings of his past life.

15
01:50:31,578 --> 01:50:37,578
The King premiered at the 76th Venice International Film Festival on 2 September
2019, and was released digitally via Netflix on 11 October 2019.

16
01:57:53,684 --> 01:57:59,684
The film received favourable reviews from film critics but, despite being presented as an adaptation of Shakespeare's Henriad rather than as a
historical documentary film, was criticised by historians for historical inaccuracies and for deviating from the original plays.

